{"date": "2026-10-27", "word": "Flat", "summary": "A flat day (forecast light). Thermals stayed flat all day. The upslope ran from about 07:45 to about 16:00. A low day for October: the base stayed down near 3,500 ft (normal 4,500\u20135,400 ft). The evening before, the page called it low, a hit. Midday the base averaged about 3,500 ft by the Kekoa camera; the morning update said about 4,200 ft, off by 700 ft. Most of the day the shear line was north of Pukalani, reaching the coast near Haiku; furthest south about 08:22, crossing Kula Highway between the middle Lower Kula Road junction and Waiakoa. Data gaps: no readings all day from 1 station (Nakula); Kahikinui stopped at 13:55; the Mesonet could not be reached on 17 of 60 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Flat</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the NAM sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Light</div>", "base": "", "notes": [], "chart": "<div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase, derived</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#2a78d6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Derived (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#3f9d5a;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Kekoa camera</span></div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;width:100%;min-width:0;height:220px\"><canvas id=\"basechart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Derived cloudbase through the day\"></canvas></div>\n<div class=\"sub\">Derived from the stations every 15 minutes during the upslope.</div>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var d = {\"derived\": [[540, 4450.0], [555, 4500.0], [570, 4680.0], [585, 4800.0], [600, 4790.0], [615, 4850.0], [630, 4940.0], [645, 5030.0], [660, 4690.0], [675, 4610.0], [690, 4180.0], [705, 3990.0], [720, 3530.0], [735, 3460.0], [750, 3340.0], [765, 3410